#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:32
msgid ""
"It makes its nest in a giant tree in the\n"
"forest. It ferociously guards against\n"
"anything nearing its territory. It is said\n"
"to be the protector of the forest's trees."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:103
msgid ""
"Leaves grow out of this Pokémon's body.\n"
"They help obscure a Grovyle from the eyes\n"
"of its enemies while it is in a thickly\n"
"overgrown forest."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:179
msgid ""
"In the jungle, its power is without equal.\n"
"This Pokémon carefully grows trees and\n"
"plants. It regulates its body temperature\n"
"by basking in sunlight."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:253
msgid ""
"Thanks to the power in its quick legs,\n"
"Mega Sceptile can be on its opponent in a\n"
"flash. It can cut off a portion of its tail\n"
"to fire it like a missile at an opponent."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:324
msgid ""
"If attacked, it strikes back by spitting\n"
"balls of fire it forms in its stomach.\n"
"A Torchic dislikes darkness because it\n"
"can't see its surroundings."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:409
msgid ""
"It lashes out with 10 kicks per second.\n"
"Its strong fighting instinct compels it\n"
"to keep up its offensive until the\n"
"opponent gives up."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:496
msgid ""
"It learns martial arts that use punches\n"
"and kicks. Every several years, its old\n"
"feathers burn off, and new, supple\n"
"feathers grow back in their place."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:585
msgid ""
"As it unleashes a flurry of savage kicks,\n"
"its legs can begin to burn from the\n"
"friction of the surrounding atmosphere.\n"
"They're always a source of pride to it."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:656
msgid ""
"On land, it can powerfully lift large\n"
"boulders by planting its four feet and\n"
"heaving. It sleeps by burying itself in soil\n"
"at the water's edge."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:727
msgid ""
"Its toughened hind legs enable it to stand\n"
"upright. Because it weakens if its skin\n"
"dries out, it replenishes fluids by playing\n"
"in mud."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:807
msgid ""
"If it senses the approach of a storm and\n"
"a tidal wave, it protects its seaside nest\n"
"by piling up boulders. It swims as fast as\n"
"a jet ski."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:883
msgid ""
"When it Mega Evolves, the strength that it\n"
"needs to act in the water is increased.\n"
"It can use its tenacious power\n"
"both on land and in the water."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:964
msgid ""
"It savagely threatens foes with bared\n"
"fangs. It chases after fleeing targets\n"
"tenaciously. It turns tail and runs,\n"
"however, if the foe strikes back."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1037
msgid ""
"In the wild, Mightyena live in a pack.\n"
"They never defy their leader's orders.\n"
"They defeat foes with perfectly\n"
"coordinated teamwork."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1120
msgid ""
"Rubbing its nose against the ground, it\n"
"always wanders about back and forth in\n"
"search of something. It is distinguished\n"
"by the zigzag footprints it leaves."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1198
msgid ""
"It is exceedingly fast if it only has to run\n"
"in a straight line. When it spots pond-\n"
"dwelling prey underwater, it quickly leaps\n"
"in and catches it with its sharp claws."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1269
msgid ""
"Its restlessness has it constantly moving\n"
"in zigzags. It will purposely run into other\n"
"Pokémon to start fights. It's thought to\n"
"be the oldest form of Zigzagoon."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1336
msgid ""
"This very aggressive Pokémon will\n"
"recklessly challenge opponents stronger\n"
"than itself. It uses its long tongue to\n"
"taunt them to then tackle forcefully."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1402
msgid ""
"Its voice is staggering in volume.\n"
"Obstagoon has a tendency to take on a\n"
"threatening posture and shout--this move\n"
"is known as Obstruct."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1476
msgid ""
"It sticks to tree branches and eats\n"
"leaves. The thread it spits from its mouth,\n"
"which becomes gooey when it touches\n"
"air, slows the movement of its foes."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1547
msgid ""
"It prepares for evolution using the\n"
"energy it stored while it was a Wurmple.\n"
"It keeps watch over the surroundings with\n"
"its two eyes."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1625
msgid ""
"Its colorfully patterned wings are its\n"
"most prominent feature. It flies through\n"
"flower-covered fields collecting pollen.\n"
"It attacks ferociously when angered."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1719
msgid ""
"To avoid detection by its enemies, it hides\n"
"motionlessly beneath large leaves and in\n"
"the gaps of branches. It also attaches\n"
"dead leaves to its body for camouflage."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1801
msgid ""
"It is a nocturnal Pokémon that flies from\n"
"fields and mountains to the attraction of\n"
"streetlights at night. It looses highly\n"
"toxic powder from its wings."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1897
msgid ""
"This Pokémon lives in ponds with clean\n"
"water. It is known to ferry small Pokémon\n"
"across ponds by carrying them on the\n"
"broad leaf on its head."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1968
msgid ""
"In the evening, it takes great delight in\n"
"popping out of rivers and startling people.\n"
"It feeds on aquatic moss that grows on\n"
"rocks in the riverbed."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2045
msgid ""
"When it hears festive music, all the cells\n"
"in its body become stimulated, and it\n"
"begins moving in rhythm. It does not\n"
"quail even when it faces a tough opponent."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2132
msgid ""
"It hangs off branches and absorbs\n"
"nutrients. When it finishes eating, its\n"
"body becomes so heavy that it drops to\n"
"the ground with a thump."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2208
msgid ""
"A forest-dwelling Pokémon that is skilled\n"
"at climbing trees. Its long and pointed\n"
"nose is its weak point. It loses power if\n"
"the nose is gripped."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2306
msgid ""
"It is said to arrive on chilly, wintry winds.\n"
"Feared from long ago as the guardian of\n"
"forests, this Pokémon lives in a deep\n"
"forest where people do not venture."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2388
msgid ""
"Although it is small, it is very courageous.\n"
"It will take on a larger Skarmory on an\n"
"equal footing. However, its will weakens if\n"
"it becomes hungry."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2470
msgid ""
"A Swellow dives upon prey from far above.\n"
"It never misses its targets. It takes to\n"
"the skies in search of lands with a warm\n"
"climate."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2544
msgid ""
"It makes its nest on a sheer cliff at the\n"
"edge of the sea. It has trouble keeping\n"
"its wings flapping in flight. Instead, it\n"
"soars on updrafts."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2625
msgid ""
"It skims the tops of waves as it flies.\n"
"When it spots prey, it uses its large beak\n"
"to scoop up the victim with water.\n"
"It protects its eggs in its beak."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2709
msgid ""
"A Ralts has the power to sense the\n"
"emotions of people and Pokémon with the\n"
"horns on its head. It takes cover if it\n"
"senses any hostility."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2778
msgid ""
"A Kirlia has the psychic power to create \n"
"a rip in the dimensions and see into the\n"
"future. It is said to dance with pleasure\n"
"on sunny mornings."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2856
msgid ""
"It apparently does not feel the pull of\n"
"gravity because it supports itself with\n"
"psychic power. It will give its life to\n"
"protect its Trainer."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2930
msgid ""
"By opening its heart, Mega Gardevoir\n"
"becomes able to use tremendous psychic\n"
"power. The red plate in its chest is said to\n"
"be a physical manifestation of its heart."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3010
msgid ""
"A master of courtesy and swordsmanship,\n"
"it fights using extending swords on its\n"
"elbows when trying to protect someone.\n"
"It can sense what its foe is thinking."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3083
msgid ""
"Mega Gallade has a knightly appearance.\n"
"It can use its psychic power to reshape\n"
"both arms into blades simultaneously and\n"
"fight using a dual-wielding style."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3156
msgid ""
"They gather on puddles after evening\n"
"downpours, gliding across the surface\n"
"of water as if sliding. It secretes honey\n"
"with a sweet aroma from its head."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3235
msgid ""
"It intimidates foes with the large eyelike\n"
"patterns on its antennae. Because it can't\n"
"fly if its wings get wet, it shelters itself\n"
"from rain under large trees and eaves."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3318
msgid ""
"It loves to eat damp, composted soil in\n"
"forests. If you enter a forest after a\n"
"long rain, you can see many Shroomish\n"
"feasting on composted soil."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3401
msgid ""
"It scatters spores from holes in the cap\n"
"on its head. It loves warm and humid\n"
"climates. It feeds on trees and plants in\n"
"fields and forests."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3472
msgid ""
"It sleeps virtually all day and night long.\n"
"It doesn't change its nest its entire life,\n"
"but it sometimes travels great distances\n"
"by swimming in rivers."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3544
msgid ""
"It can't keep still because its blood boils\n"
"with energy. It runs through the fields\n"
"and mountains all day to calm itself. If it\n"
"doesn't, it can't sleep at night."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3622
msgid ""
"Hordes of Slaking gather around trees\n"
"when fruits come into season. They wait\n"
"around patiently for ripened fruits to fall\n"
"out of the trees."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3696
msgid ""
"It makes its nest at the roots of a mighty\n"
"tree. Using its whiskerlike antennae, it\n"
"probes its surroundings in the\n"
"pitch-black darkness of soil."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3772
msgid ""
"Because it darts about vigorously at high\n"
"speed, it is very difficult to see. Hearing\n"
"its distinctive cries for too long induces\n"
"a headache."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3855
msgid ""
"A peculiar Pokémon that floats in air even\n"
"though its wings remain completely still.\n"
"The inside of its body is hollow and\n"
"utterly dark."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3927
msgid ""
"Its cries equal a jet plane in volume.\n"
"It inhales through its ear canals. Because\n"
"of this system, it can cry continually\n"
"without having to catch its breath."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4003
msgid ""
"It positions the round speakers on its\n"
"head to assail foes with ultrasonic waves\n"
"at massive volume. It builds power by\n"
"stomping the ground."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4081
msgid ""
"It has sound-generating organs all over\n"
"its body. It communicates with others by\n"
"adjusting the tone and volume of the cries\n"
"it emits."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4151
msgid ""
"It loves to toughen up its body above all\n"
"else. If you hear quaking rumbles in a cave,\n"
"it is the sound of Makuhita undertaking\n"
"strenuous training."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4227
msgid ""
"It has the habit of challenging others\n"
"without hesitation to tests of strength.\n"
"It's been known to stand on train tracks\n"
"and stop trains using forearm thrusts."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4298
msgid ""
"Its body emits a powerful magnetism.\n"
"It feeds on prey that is pulled in by the\n"
"force. Its magnetism is stronger in cold\n"
"seasons."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4377
msgid ""
"It freely controls three units called\n"
"Mini-Noses using magnetic force.\n"
"With them, it can attack its foes from\n"
"three directions."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4454
msgid ""
"A Skitty's adorably cute behavior makes it\n"
"highly popular. In battle, it makes its tail\n"
"puff out. It threatens foes with a sharp\n"
"growl."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4534
msgid ""
"Rather than keeping a permanent lair,\n"
"it habitually seeks comfortable spots and\n"
"sleeps there. It is nocturnal and becomes\n"
"active at dusk."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4609
msgid ""
"It digs branching holes in caves using its\n"
"sharp claws in search of food--raw gems.\n"
"A Sableye lurks in darkness and is seen\n"
"only rarely."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4687
msgid ""
"Bathed in the energy of Mega Evolution,\n"
"the gemstone on its chest expands, rips\n"
"through its skin, and falls out."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4765
msgid ""
"Its giant jaws are actually steel horns\n"
"that transformed. It fools foes into\n"
"complacency with its adorable gestures,\n"
"then chomps them with its huge jaws."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4845
msgid ""
"Its two sets of jaws thrash about\n"
"violently as if they each had a will of\n"
"their own. One gnash from them can turn a\n"
"boulder to dust."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4918
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that is clad in steel armor.\n"
"A new suit of armor is made when it evolves.\n"
"The old, discarded armor is salvaged as\n"
"metal for making iron products."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4990
msgid ""
"When two Lairon meet in the wild, they\n"
"fight for territory by bashing into each\n"
"other with their steel bodies. The sound\n"
"of their collision carries for miles."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5067
msgid ""
"Its iron horns grow longer a little at\n"
"a time. They are used to determine the\n"
"Aggron's age. The gouges in its armor are\n"
"worn with pride as mementos from battles."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5142
msgid ""
"When Aggron Mega Evolves into\n"
"Mega Aggron, the destructive ability of\n"
"its fearsome horns can turn a steel-clad\n"
"tank into so much scrap metal."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5213
msgid ""
"It continually meditates for hours every\n"
"day. As a result of rigorous and dedicated\n"
"yoga training, it has tempered its\n"
"spiritual power so much it can fly."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5295
msgid ""
"Through crushingly harsh yoga training, it\n"
"gained the power to foretell its foe's\n"
"actions. It battles with elegant, dance-\n"
"like movement."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5386
msgid ""
"It uses its amped-up willpower to create\n"
"additional arms for itself. The more it\n"
"has trained its spirit, the more realistic\n"
"and dexterous these arms become."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5457
msgid ""
"It generates electricity using friction\n"
"from the atmosphere. In seasons with\n"
"especially arid air, its entire body blazes\n"
"with violent showers of sparks."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5528
msgid ""
"Because lightning falls in their vicinities,\n"
"Manectric were thought to have been born\n"
"from lightning. In battle, they create\n"
"thunderclouds."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5604
msgid ""
"Too much electricity has built up in its\n"
"body, irritating Manectric. Its explosive\n"
"speed is equal to that of a lightning bolt."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5679
msgid ""
"It has the trait of cheering on its fellow\n"
"Pokémon. By shorting out the electricity\n"
"it releases from its paws, it creates\n"
"pom-poms for cheering."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5756
msgid ""
"At a meeting of Pokémon academics, it was\n"
"announced that simultaneous exposure to\n"
"electricity from a Plusle and Minun will\n"
"promote circulation and boost vitality."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5835
msgid ""
"With their taillights lit, Volbeat fly in\n"
"a swarm, drawing geometric designs in the\n"
"night sky. They move their nests if their\n"
"pond water becomes dirty."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5918
msgid ""
"A nocturnal Pokémon that becomes active\n"
"upon nightfall. It leads a Volbeat swarm\n"
"to draw patterns in the night sky. Over 200\n"
"different patterns have been confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5993
msgid ""
"Over the winter, it closes its bud and\n"
"endures the cold. Sensitive to changing\n"
"temperature, the bud is said to bloom\n"
"when it feels the sun's warm touch."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6065
msgid ""
"A Roselia that drinks nutritionally rich\n"
"springwater blooms with lovely flowers.\n"
"The fragrance of its flowers has the\n"
"effect of making its foes careless."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6160
msgid ""
"Its sweet aroma attracts prey.\n"
"With the movements of a dancer,\n"
"it strikes with whips that are densely\n"
"lined with poison thorns."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6244
msgid ""
"This Pokémon's stomach fluid can even\n"
"digest scrap iron. In one gulp, it can\n"
"swallow something that is as large as\n"
"itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6330
msgid ""
"Its powerful stomach acid is capable of\n"
"digesting almost anything. The one thing\n"
"in the whole world a Swalot can't digest is\n"
"its own stomach."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6414
msgid ""
"Carvanha attack ships in swarms, making\n"
"them sink. Although it is said to be a very\n"
"vicious Pokémon, it timidly flees as soon\n"
"as it finds itself alone."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6490
msgid ""
"The vicious and sly gangster of the sea.\n"
"Its skin is specially textured to minimize\n"
"drag in water. Its speed tops out at over\n"
"75 miles per hour."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6571
msgid ""
"The yellow patterns it bears are old scars.\n"
"The energy from Mega Evolution runs\n"
"through them, causing it sharp pain and\n"
"suffering."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6643
msgid ""
"While this Pokémon usually lives in the sea,\n"
"it can survive on land, although not too\n"
"long. It loses vitality if its body becomes\n"
"dried out."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6716
msgid ""
"It breathes through nostrils that it\n"
"raises above the sea. By inhaling to its\n"
"maximum capacity, a Wailord can dive close\n"
"to 10,000 feet beneath the waves."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6790
msgid ""
"A Numel stores boiling magma in the hump\n"
"on its back. It is a hardy Pokémon that can\n"
"transport a 220-pound load. It has served\n"
"humans at work since long ago."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6879
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that lives in the crater of\n"
"a volcano. Every 10 years, the volcanoes\n"
"on its back erupt violently. Research is\n"
"under way on the cause of eruption."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6971
msgid ""
"The humps on its back have transformed\n"
"into one large and very active volcano. It\n"
"has a deep hatred of water or any moisture\n"
"and has an explosive personality."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7047
msgid ""
"It battles using energy it gets from\n"
"burning coal. When loosing smoke from its\n"
"nostrils, it lets off a sound that is\n"
"similar to a locomotive's horn."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7119
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that manipulates psychic power\n"
"at will. It doesn't stop bouncing even when\n"
"it is asleep. It loves eating mushrooms\n"
"that grow underground."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7196
msgid ""
"It stores power in the black pearls on its\n"
"forehead. When it uses psychic power, it\n"
"performs an odd dance step. Its style of\n"
"dancing became hugely popular overseas."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7273
msgid ""
"It is distinguished by a pattern of\n"
"spots that is always different. Its\n"
"unsteady, tottering walk has the\n"
"effect of fouling its foe's aim."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7356
msgid ""
"Its big jaws crunch through boulders.\n"
"Because its head is so big, it has a hard\n"
"time getting back upright if it tips over\n"
"onto its back."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7428
msgid ""
"It looses ultrasonic waves by rubbing its\n"
"wings together. Since a Vibrava's wings\n"
"are still in the process of growing, it can\n"
"only fly short distances."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7507
msgid ""
"The flapping of its wings sounds like\n"
"singing. To prevent detection by enemies,\n"
"it hides itself by flapping up a cloud of\n"
"desert sand."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7582
msgid ""
"Cacnea live in deserts with virtually no\n"
"rainfall. It battles by swinging its thick,\n"
"spiked arms. Once a year, a yellow flower\n"
"blooms."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7661
msgid ""
"After spending thousands of years in\n"
"harsh deserts, its blood transformed into\n"
"the same substances as sand. It is\n"
"nocturnal, so it hunts at night."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7743
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that has wings like cottony\n"
"clouds. After enduring winter, in which\n"
"little food is available, Swablu flocks\n"
"move closer to towns in the spring."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7817
msgid ""
"It hums in a beautiful soprano voice.\n"
"It flies among white clouds in the blue\n"
"sky. It launches intensely hot fireballs\n"
"from its mouth."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7894
msgid ""
"It sings with a voice that is even more\n"
"beautiful than before it Mega Evolved.\n"
"Its feathers became larger for protection\n"
"and glimmer with an iridescent sheen."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7968
msgid ""
"When it battles, it stands on its hind legs\n"
"and attacks with its sharply clawed\n"
"forelegs. Its fur bristles if it encounters\n"
"any Seviper."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8045
msgid ""
"Seviper and Zangoose are eternal rivals.\n"
"It counters a Zangoose's dazzling agility\n"
"with its swordlike tail, which also oozes\n"
"a horrible poison."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8127
msgid ""
"It becomes very active on the night of\n"
"a full moon. This Pokémon was first\n"
"discovered 40 years ago at the site of\n"
"a meteor strike."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8207
msgid ""
"Solar energy is the source of this \n"
"Pokémon's power. On sunny days, groups of\n"
"Solrock line up facing the sun and absorb\n"
"its light."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8283
msgid ""
"Its body is covered with a slimy film.\n"
"The film acts as a barrier to prevent germs\n"
"in muddy water from entering the\n"
"Barboach's body."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8367
msgid ""
"Mysteriously, it can foretell earthquakes.\n"
"In the daytime, it sleeps in mud at the\n"
"bottom of a pond. When it awakens, it\n"
"continually feeds throughout the night."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8446
msgid ""
"Once it grips prey with its large pincers,\n"
"it will never let go, no matter what.\n"
"It is a hardy Pokémon that can thrive\n"
"in any environment."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8519
msgid ""
"A brutish Pokémon that loves to battle.\n"
"A veteran Crawdaunt that has prevailed in\n"
"hundreds of battles has giant pincers\n"
"marked with countless scars."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8591
msgid ""
"A Baltoy moves by spinning on its single\n"
"foot. It has been depicted in murals \n"
"adorning the walls of a once-bustling city\n"
"in an ancient age."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8665
msgid ""
"A Claydol sleeps while hovering in midair.\n"
"Its arms are separate from its body.\n"
"They are kept floating by the Pokémon's\n"
"manipulation of psychic power."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8746
msgid ""
"It disguises itself as seaweed by making\n"
"its tentacles sway. Unsuspecting prey\n"
"that come too close are swallowed whole.\n"
"It became extinct 100 million years ago."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8824
msgid ""
"It drags its heavy body along the\n"
"seafloor. It makes its nest in the shallows\n"
"of warm seas. Cradily can be seen on\n"
"beaches when the tide goes out."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8903
msgid ""
"It was resurrected from a fossil using the\n"
"power of science. It swims by undulating\n"
"the eight wings at its sides. They were\n"
"feet that adapted to life in the sea."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8982
msgid ""
"Armaldo usually lives on land. However,\n"
"when it hunts for prey, it dives beneath\n"
"the ocean. It swims around using its two\n"
"large wings."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9058
msgid ""
"Feebas live in ponds that are heavily\n"
"infested with weeds. Because of its\n"
"hopelessly shabby appearance, it\n"
"seems as if few Trainers raise it."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9137
msgid ""
"It is said to live at the bottom of\n"
"large lakes. Considered to be the most\n"
"beautiful of all Pokémon, it has been\n"
"depicted in paintings and statues."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9226
msgid ""
"It alters its form depending on the\n"
"weather. Changes in the climate such as\n"
"the temperature and humidity appear to\n"
"affect its cellular structure."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9305
msgid ""
"Castform takes this form on bright days.\n"
"In an experiment where is was placed in\n"
"front of a heater, it didn't change to this\n"
"form. Its body is warm and toasty."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9386
msgid ""
"This is Castform's form while it's raining.\n"
"In an experiment where it was placed in a\n"
"shower, it didn't change to this form. Its\n"
"body is soft, slightly swollen with water."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9466
msgid ""
"This is Castform's form in a hailstorm.\n"
"In an experiment where it was placed\n"
"in a freezer, it didn't change to this form.\n"
"Its cold skin is as smooth as ice."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9549
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that has the ability to alter its\n"
"body colors to match its surroundings.\n"
"A Kecleon reverts to its original colors if\n"
"it is startled."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9627
msgid ""
"This Pokémon roams about deep in the\n"
"night seeking such negative emotions as\n"
"grudges and envy. It retreats to its nest\n"
"when the sun begins to rise."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9707
msgid ""
"An abandoned plush doll became this\n"
"Pokémon. They are said to live in garbage\n"
"dumps and wander about in search of the\n"
"children that threw them away."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9788
msgid ""
"Extraordinary energy amplifies its\n"
"cursing power to such an extent that it\n"
"can't help but curse its own Trainer."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9865
msgid ""
"A glare from its single scarlet eye makes\n"
"even burly grown-ups freeze in utter fear.\n"
"It is a nocturnal Pokémon that roams\n"
"about under the cloak of darkness."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9943
msgid ""
"It is thought that its body is hollow with\n"
"only a spectral ball of fire burning inside.\n"
"However, no one has been able to\n"
"confirm this theory as fact."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10030
msgid ""
"This feared Pokémon is said to travel to\n"
"worlds unknown. Some even believe that\n"
"it takes lost spirits into its pliant body\n"
"and guides them home."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10112
msgid ""
"It flies by flapping its broad leaves.\n"
"The bunch of fruit that grows around its\n"
"neck is deliciously sweet. In the spring,\n"
"it scatters pollen from its neck."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10186
msgid ""
"There is an orb inside its mouth.\n"
"When it hops, the orb bounces all\n"
"over and makes a ringing sound.\n"
"It can cry for an awfully long time."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10269
msgid ""
"They fly about very actively when the hot\n"
"season arrives. They communicate among\n"
"themselves using seven different and\n"
"distinguishing cries."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10359
msgid ""
"It vibrates its entire body to attack in\n"
"all directions using sound waves. Any who\n"
"hear the vibrations get so confused, they\n"
"forget who they are."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10422
msgid ""
"It sharply senses even subtle changes in\n"
"the sky and the land to predict natural\n"
"disasters. It is a long-lived Pokémon that\n"
"has a life-span of 100 years."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10501
msgid ""
"As the energy of Mega Evolution fills it,\n"
"its fur bristles. What you see on its back\n"
"are not true wings, and this Pokémon isn't\n"
"able to fly."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10577
msgid ""
"Using fur that it has made into sharp,\n"
"clawlike shapes, it cuts down foes with\n"
"a single blow. This is an act of kindness\n"
"to keep them from suffering."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10639
msgid ""
"They tend to move about in groups of\n"
"around five Snorunt. In snowy regions,\n"
"it is said that when they are seen late at\n"
"night, snowfall will arrive by morning."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10719
msgid ""
"A Glalie has the power to instantaneously\n"
"freeze moisture in the atmosphere.\n"
"A dazzling cloud of diamondlike ice\n"
"crystals forms around its body."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10796
msgid ""
"The power of Mega Evolution was so strong\n"
"that it smashed Glalie's jaw. Its inability\n"
"to eat very well leaves Glalie irritated."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10866
msgid ""
"When it finds people or Pokémon it likes,\n"
"it freezes them and takes them to its\n"
"chilly den, where they become its\n"
"decorations."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10941
msgid ""
"This Pokémon can use eerie cold\n"
"air imbued with ghost energy to\n"
"freeze even insubstantial things,\n"
"such as flames or the wind."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11003
msgid ""
"It is completely covered with plushy fur.\n"
"As a result, it never feels the cold even\n"
"when it is rolling about on ice floes or\n"
"diving in the sea."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11082
msgid ""
"Sealeo live in herds on ice floes. Using its\n"
"powerful flippers, it shatters ice.\n"
"It dives into the sea to hunt prey five\n"
"times a day."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11162
msgid ""
"To protect its herd, the leader battles\n"
"anything that invades its territory, even\n"
"at the cost of its life. Its tusks may snap\n"
"off in battle."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11235
msgid ""
"A Clamperl slams its shell closed on prey\n"
"to prevent escape. The pearl it creates\n"
"upon evolution is said to be infused with\n"
"a mysterious energy."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11311
msgid ""
"To withstand the crushing pressure of\n"
"water deep under the sea, its spine is very\n"
"thick and sturdy. Its tail, which is shaped\n"
"like a small fish, has eyes that light up."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11381
msgid ""
"A Gorebyss siphons the body fluids of prey\n"
"through its thin, tubular mouth. Its light\n"
"pink body color turns vivid when it\n"
"finishes feeding."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11454
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that was once believed to have\n"
"been extinct. The species has not changed\n"
"its form for 100 million years. It walks on\n"
"the seafloor using its pectoral fins."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11540
msgid ""
"Luvdisc make the branches of Corsola\n"
"their nests. There is a custom from long\n"
"ago of giving a Luvdisc as a gift to\n"
"express one's feelings of love."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11613
msgid ""
"Although it is small, this Pokémon is very\n"
"powerful because its body is a bundle of\n"
"muscles. It launches head-butts with its\n"
"ironlike skull."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11685
msgid ""
"It hardly eats while it awaits evolution.\n"
"It becomes hardier by enduring hunger.\n"
"Its shell peels off the instant it begins\n"
"to evolve."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11762
msgid ""
"After many long years, its cellular\n"
"structure underwent a sudden mutation to\n"
"grow wings. When angered, it loses all\n"
"thought and rampages out of control."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11840
msgid ""
"Mega Evolution fuels its brutality, and it\n"
"may even turn on the Trainer who raised it.\n"
"It's been dubbed the blood-soaked.\n"
"crescent."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11913
msgid ""
"When Beldum gather in a swarm, they move\n"
"in perfect unison as if they were but one\n"
"Pokémon. They communicate with each other\n"
"using brain waves."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11986
msgid ""
"The claws tipping its arms pack the\n"
"destructive power to tear through thick\n"
"iron sheets as if they were silk. It flies\n"
"at over 60 miles per hour."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12063
msgid ""
"Metagross has four brains that are joined\n"
"by a complex neural network. As a result of\n"
"integration, this Pokémon is smarter than\n"
"a supercomputer."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12140
msgid ""
"When it knows it can't win, it digs the\n"
"claws on its legs into its opponent and\n"
"starts the countdown to a big explosion."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12218
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that is made entirely of rocks\n"
"and boulders. If parts of its body chip off\n"
"in battle, Regirock repairs itself by\n"
"adding new rocks."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12297
msgid ""
"Its entire body is made of Antarctic ice.\n"
"After extensive studies, researchers\n"
"believe the ice was formed during an\n"
"ice age."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12377
msgid ""
"Its body is harder than any other kind of\n"
"metal. The body metal is composed of a\n"
"mysterious substance. Not only is it hard,\n"
"it shrinks and stretches flexibly."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12456
msgid ""
"They make a small herd of only several\n"
"members. They rarely make contact with\n"
"people or other Pokémon. They disappear\n"
"if they sense enemies."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12535
msgid ""
"Its body is smaller than Mega Latios's\n"
"body. It is more agile and can make very\n"
"sharp turns. When it Mega Evolves, its\n"
"defensive strength grows substantially."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12615
msgid ""
"Even in hiding, it can detect the locations\n"
"of others and sense their emotions since\n"
"it has telepathy. Its intelligence allows\n"
"it to understand human languages."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12694
msgid ""
"It's larger than Mega Latias, and can\n"
"achieve higher speeds in flight.\n"
"This Pokémon can use its speed in battle\n"
"to unleash a flurry of attacks."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12774
msgid ""
"Kyogre has appeared in mythology as the\n"
"creator of the sea. After long years of\n"
"feuding with Groudon, it took to sleep at\n"
"the bottom of the sea."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12849
msgid ""
"When Kyogre roared, water poured forth\n"
"and the seas spread outward.\n"
"Dark clouds enshrouded the world,\n"
"and the deluge fell upon all…"
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12929
msgid ""
"Groudon has appeared in mythology as the\n"
"creator of the land. It sleeps in magma\n"
"underground and is said to make volcanoes\n"
"erupt on awakening."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13004
msgid ""
"When Groudon howled, the earth swelled and\n"
"the land grew wide. The sun blazed atop\n"
"and all the world around the creature\n"
"was enveloped in incandescent heat."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13085
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that flies endlessly in the\n"
"ozone layer. It is said it would descend\n"
"to the ground if Kyogre and Groudon\n"
"were to fight."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13163
msgid ""
"Particles stream from the filaments that\n"
"extend from its jaw. They can control the\n"
"density and humidity of the air, allowing\n"
"Rayquaza to manipulate the weather."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13246
msgid ""
"Jirachi is said to make wishes come true.\n"
"While it sleeps, a tough crystalline shell\n"
"envelops the body to protect it from\n"
"enemies."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13336
msgid ""
"Deoxys emerged from a virus that came\n"
"from space. It is highly intelligent and\n"
"can shoot lasers from the crystalline\n"
"organ on its chest."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13416
msgid ""
"This Deoxys has transformed into its\n"
"aggressive guise. It can fool enemies\n"
"by altering its appearance."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13494
msgid ""
"When it changes form, an aurora\n"
"appears. It absorbs attacks by\n"
"altering its cellular structure."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13573
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that mutated from an\n"
"extraterrestrial virus exposed to a laser\n"
"beam. Its body is configured for superior \n"
"agility and speed."
msgstr ""

